{"kind":"report","text":"C1 ruling on 87ff769f: both proposals stand. C1 stays parked under order afdebb86; this ruling holds when it resumes in phase 3.\n\n1. Keep the max4096 text field. The native bad-field refusal, with its text-field detail, is the named refusal that the sales note's \"a longer text ... is refused by name\" asks for. Assert bad-field at that boundary, and calendar-post-limit for the twenty-fifth post. Add no calendar-text-limit form.\n2. The six-kibibyte bound applies to each row of the complete carousel source, and the 24-post quarter source stays at or under 144 KiB. The note derives 144 KiB from 24 rows of six kibibytes, so the bound belongs to the list rows. The selected post record reads its four-kibibyte body separately, inside the native 256 KiB query limit. Witness each list row at or under six kibibytes and the whole unfiltered quarter source at or under 144 KiB. Report the selected-card size separately. Add no six-kibibyte limit on the selected record."}